.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt SWITCHBOARDCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm switchboardctl
.Nd control and inspect switchboard
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | services | reload | bundles
.Nm
.Cm start | stop | restart | cache-status Ar label
.Nm
.Cm enable | disable Ar bundle
.Nm
.Cm install Oo Fl -personal Oc Ar path.cap
.Nm
.Cm verify Oo Fl -personal Oc Ar path.cap ...
.Nm
.Cm deps Ar program
.Nm
.Cm graph Op Fl -text | Fl -dot | Fl -json
.Op Fl -lint
.Op Fl -root Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the administrative client for
.Xr switchboard 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "verify path.cap ..."
.It Cm status
Show daemon and service state.
.It Cm cache-status Ar label
Report executable mappings of the system library cache in a supervised unit.
SwitchBoard queries its child using existing launcher protection authority;
the caller receives counters, not addresses or debug authority.
The selected generation is identified by device and inode, so a renamed cache
is still recognized and an unrelated file with the same name is excluded.
The loader's read-only index mapping is not counted.
Virtual mapped bytes are not resident memory or measured savings.
An unavailable process or denied observation is an error, not a zero count.
This command requires an attributed control grant, like status.
.It Cm services
List loaded service runtimes.
Each running unit also shows
.Ql coal=
(its kernel coalition id) and
.Ql resp=
(who it exists on behalf of, with that coalition's id):
.Ql switchboard
for boot-launched and operator-started units,
.Ql self
for a shared provider activated on demand,
the requesting unit's label for a private helper or a per-user unit
started by another unit of the same owner.
Software attributes do not establish a login-session coalition.
.Pp
A service waiting for resource teardown also shows
.Ql cleanup= ,
.Ql child= ,
.Ql coalition= ,
and
.Ql observed=
fields.
.Ql cleanup=blocked
includes a numeric and textual
.Ql cleanup-error .
A timeout keeps replacement blocked; a retained observer can still report
completion later.
An authorized start during pending cleanup returns
.Er EBUSY .
Stop records the request to suppress automatic restart but does not assert
that cleanup has finished.
There is no command to force unconfirmed cleanup to count as complete.
.It Cm tree
Show the responsibility tree: every running unit indented under the
coalition it answers to, starting from the switchboard's own root
coalition and the self-rooted providers.
The header carries the kernel's boot id
.Pq Va kern.boot_id :
coalition ids are unique within one boot only, and the switchboard start
audit record pairs the same boot id with the root coalition id so records
from different boots are never confused.
The ids shown are the same ones
.Xr ps 1
prints with
.Fl o Cm coal,rcoal,rpid
and
.Xr procstat 1
prints with
.Cm coalition ,
so process attribution can be correlated independently of authorization.
.It Cm reload
Transactionally rescan bundles, validate the dependency graph, and apply
additions, changes, and removals.
Requires the
.Dq Li system.switchboard.admin
attribute on the calling executable's software policy
.Pq Xr switchboard 5 .
A UNIX UID alone does not supply this attribute.
.It Cm start Ar label
Start a loaded stopped unit immediately and reset its restart backoff.
Requires the
.Dq Li system.switchboard.admin
attribute on the calling executable's software policy
.Pq Xr switchboard 5 .
A UNIX UID alone does not supply this attribute.
.It Cm stop Ar label
Gracefully stop a runtime, escalating after its configured timeout.
Requires the
.Dq Li system.switchboard.admin
attribute on the calling executable's software policy
.Pq Xr switchboard 5 .
A UNIX UID alone does not supply this attribute.
.It Cm restart Ar label
Stop the unit and then start it again, driving the same control operations as
.Cm stop
and
.Cm start .
A unit that is already stopped is simply started.
Requires the
.Dq Li system.switchboard.admin
attribute on the calling executable's software policy
.Pq Xr switchboard 5 .
A UNIX UID alone does not supply this attribute.
.It Cm enable Ar bundle
Remove
.Ar bundle
from the persistent operator disable list and apply the change immediately by
reloading, so the bundle's units are launched.
Requires the
.Dq Li system.switchboard.admin
attribute on the calling executable's software policy
.Pq Xr switchboard 5 .
A UNIX UID alone does not supply this attribute.
.It Cm disable Ar bundle
Record
.Ar bundle
in the persistent operator disable list and apply the change immediately by
reloading, so its units are stopped and not relaunched across reboots until
re-enabled.
Requires the
.Dq Li system.switchboard.admin
attribute on the calling executable's software policy
.Pq Xr switchboard 5 .
A UNIX UID alone does not supply this attribute.
.It Cm install Oo Fl -personal Oc Ar path.cap
Verify and copy a bundle into
.Pa /Capabilities
as a root-owned global policy tree; the bundle is installed once its directory is in
place.
.Ev SWITCHBOARD_LIFECYCLE_ROOT
selects an offline root and defaults to
.Pa / .
Requires root and honors the system signature requirement.
.Pp
With
.Fl -personal ,
install for the current real UID under
.Pa /Capabilities/Users/UID/Agents .
The account directory must already be provisioned by an administrator, owned by
that UID, and not writable by group or others.
The parent Capabilities and Users directories must be root-owned and not writable
by group or others.
The tool creates Agents if absent; it cannot select another account or a global
destination, and refuses changed real/effective credentials.
Personal bundle files must have safe modes; signed modes are preserved exactly.
Existing versions are never overwritten.
An authorized reload is needed before discovery.
.It Cm verify Oo Fl -personal Oc Ar path.cap ...
Strictly validate bundle structure, manifests, executables, unique provided
names, and the combined dependency graph.
The printed effective view shows activation and local descriptors.
With
.Fl -personal ,
unsigned bundles are accepted even on signed systems; present signatures must
still verify using their embedded public keys.
Personal signatures establish integrity, not platform trust.
Services must declare control=user and domain=user; exec applications declare
domain=user and have no control field.
Platform grants, non-default credential overrides, ambient execution, global
visibility and privileged socket activation are rejected.
The parser's default account placeholders are resolved to the installation owner
by Switchboard; they do not grant that default account's credentials.
Default verification retains system trust policy.
.It Cm deps Ar program
Inspect an ELF program and print an advisory
.Va descriptors
object for linked FileSystemCmp, NetworkCmp, and CryptoCmp clients.
Global service libraries require no manifest declaration and are ignored.
.It Cm bundles
List bundles installed in
.Pa /Capabilities/System
and
.Pa /Capabilities .
.It Cm graph Oo Fl -text | Fl -dot | Fl -json Oc Oo Fl -lint Oc Oo Fl -root Ar dir Oc
Draw static software attribute coverage from the bundle registry on disk.
No running
.Xr switchboard 8
is consulted.
The nodes are declared software units, including exec-only applications, in
.Pa /Capabilities/System
and
.Pa /Capabilities
.Po or the single directory named by
.Fl -root
.Pc
and the endpoints those units publish.
User accounts and login sessions do not contribute attributes.
.Pp
An edge runs from a consumer to an endpoint when the endpoint is open
or the consumer declares every attribute the endpoint requires.
Attributes held by separate software units are never combined.
A unit never reaches its own endpoints.
This is a static coverage graph; runtime admission also depends on executable
identity, active policy, provider state, and discovery visibility.
Units are shown as
.Ar bundle-id Ns / Ns Ar unit .
.Pp
.Fl -text ,
the default, prints one line per edge,
.Dq Li CONSUMER -> ENDPOINT [open]
or
.Dq Li CONSUMER -> ENDPOINT [via a.b,c.d] ,
followed by a summary line.
.Fl -dot
prints a Graphviz digraph: units as boxes, endpoints
as nodes labelled with their name and requires, providers joined to their
endpoints by dotted lines, and attributed edges labelled with the names.
.Fl -json
prints an object with the keys
.Li units , endpoints , edges
and
.Li warnings ,
in that order, sorted so that identical registries print identical output.
.Pp
.Fl -lint
reports warnings, which the JSON form always includes under
.Li warnings :
a required attribute that no unit declares, a combination of required attributes
that no single client holds, a declaration no published endpoint requires,
or duplicate endpoint names.
These are static policy diagnostics; the graph does not infer grants from UNIX
root, groups, or an old principal-policy file.
With
.Fl -lint
the exit status is 2 when any warning was reported; text mode prints the
warnings before the summary and DOT mode prints them on standard error.
Without
.Fl -lint
the exit status is 0 whenever the registry parsed.
.Pp
The environment variables
.Ev SWITCHBOARD_BUNDLE_DIR_SYSTEM ,
.Ev SWITCHBOARD_BUNDLE_DIR_USER
and
.Ev SWITCHBOARD_PRINCIPAL_POLICY
override the registry directories and the policy file.
.El
.Sh PERSONAL NAMESPACES
System and Apps bundles share the global namespace.
Personal bundles are indexed separately for each authenticated installation
owner, so two users may install the same bundle identity and service labels.
An unqualified service label selects a global service first, then the calling
user's personal service.
Use
.Dq user:UID:label
with start, stop, restart or cache-status to select a personal service
explicitly.
Only its owner or a caller with the existing operator grant may manage it;
a numeric UID of zero alone does not confer that grant.
Status prints this qualified form for personal services.
.Pp
The operator enable and disable commands accept
.Dq user:UID:bundle-id
for personal bundles.
The unqualified bundle identity continues to affect only global bundles.
The persistent disable file still requires its existing filesystem permission
and reload requires its existing control grant.
Personal installation changes are applied by an explicit reload;
automatic install-folder watches currently cover System and Apps.
.Pp
Personal namespaces do not require code signing.
Kernel-stamped sender credentials select personal service discovery.
A signature or a caller-supplied label does not select another user's namespace
or grant system attributes.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# switchboardctl verify /path/to/MyApp.cap
# switchboardctl install /path/to/MyApp.cap
# switchboardctl reload
# switchboardctl graph --lint
# switchboardctl graph --dot | dot -Tsvg > attributes.svg
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr switchboard 5 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
